From: Robert Kirby <rkirby@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:29:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(inference): guard zero-token prefill logprob append;
 detect every model EOS when splicing the un-retokenized prefix

Two fixes carried over from the work already validated on the fork-915
branch (swe_915 workspace), re-applied here since this target has no
common ancestry with that fork and neither commit exists upstream at
1e7598cb.

1. dynamic_engine.py: the same zero-generated-tokens guard as PR #7256
   (3972b96bb), confirmed absent at this target. request_log_probs[-1] on
   an empty list crashes a prefill request that produced no generated
   tokens.

2. chat_completions.py: same substance as the fork-915 port of PR #7598
   (8381dbb97) -- EOS detection from eod/eos_id + generation_config
   (single int or list) instead of a single tokenizer.eos_id, and the
   splice boundary found by counting EOS occurrences in the retokenized
   prefix and taking the matching ordinal scanning forward, instead of a
   backward scan for the last EOS -- but hand-adapted rather than copied:
   this file has diverged substantially from the fork (multimodal media-slot
   handling, compact_prompt_token_ids, a different prior-turn tokenization
   path), though _replace_prefix_tokens itself is byte-identical to the
   fork's pre-fix version, confirmed by diff. The call site's EOS derivation
   and the previously-unguarded _replace_prefix_tokens call get the same
   try/except-and-fall-back-to-retokenized-prompt treatment as fork-915.
   Behavior re-verified: single-EOS and multi-EOS splice cases both match
   the fork-915 fix's output exactly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
